cuems-utils (0.1.1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  NOT YET BUILT FOR RELEASE. The coordinated xml-refactor landing: every
  CUEMS repository moves to its own next stable minor (cuems-utils feature
  016, specs/planning/coordinated-release-version-bump.md). This entry folds
  the never-released 0.1.0rc16 entry below: 0.1.0rc16 was since released
  from the debian/bookworm line with none of this content, so that number
  stays with the build that shipped under it.

  * Version 0.1.1, cut directly (no 0.1.1~rc1). The deprecated surface that
    0.1.0 still ships now goes away in v0.1.2 (REMOVAL_RELEASE), and every
    consumer bounds this package >= 0.1.1, << 0.1.2~.
  * Breaks: cuems-common (<< 1.3.1~), was (<< 1.3.0-23~): cuems-common
    1.3.0-23, -24 and -25 were released without the /etc/cuems handover, so
    the old bound admitted them.
  * postinst reshapes /etc/cuems before anything reads it: a field node's
    settings.xml and mappings are in the pre-013 device shape, which the
    load path refuses, and the services read them at start. Runs
    cuems-reshape-devices over the documents directly in /etc/cuems only
    (never the show library), before cuems-init-node, under a 60 s timeout,
    and warns instead of failing (cuems-utils 010 T040).
  * Migration backups never overwrite each other: cuems-reshape-devices and
    cuems-convert-documents, run in order inside one second, used to lose
    the backup of the original. cuems-convert-documents gains --check.
  * Reconciled with debian/bookworm at 398a9cf (0.1.0rc17): absorbs
    0.1.0rc15, rc16, rc16+1 and rc17 (cuems-utils feature 017), merged with
    their history, so the release line is an ancestor of this version:
    - stop_project ActionType (rc17, 869fhjdq5): the authored end of an
      unattended show. A project saved by an rc17 cluster with such a cue
      loads on 0.1.1 after cuems-reshape-devices + cuems-convert-documents;
    - media guards (rc16, 869fej07m): MediaCue.media_status(); get_media
      raises a named ValueError for a media block without a file and skips
      a missing one with a warning; get_own_media never raises;
    - stored media values pixel_width, pixel_height, file_size, file_md5
      (rc15, 869fat84r), carried by 0.1.1's own media block; an uppercase
      md5 is refused rather than lowercased;
    - Replaces: cuems-engine (<< 0.1.0rc6-2~) for cffi-gen-src (rc15);
    - no /usr/lib/cuems/CACHEDIR.TAG in the package (rc16+1).
  * stop_project takes no target: a None target is accepted at construction
    and from JSON, written as <action_target />, and loads clean. A target
    left on a stop_project cue is repaired to None on load (reported) and
    refused on save. Every other action type still requires a target.
  * pause_project and resume_project are retired from ActionType (11
    values): project pause/resume is deferred to a future release, and no
    producer ever wrote either value.
  * cuems-reshape-devices and cuems-convert-documents report every document
    the loader would refuse after they wrote it ("refused on load"); what
    they write and their exit status are unchanged.
    python -m cuemsutils.xml.reshape_devices now runs the tool.
  * Request/reply services keep answering: a request whose processor
    raised, or that was not JSON, ended NngRequestResponse.reply() for good,
    and an unencodable response was never sent, so requesters waited
    forever. Every request now gets exactly one reply, on failure
    {"OK": false, "error": "<Type>: <message>"}. The context API
    (responder_get_request) answers a malformed request the same way.
  * Communicator accepts an ipc:// address; it used to sys.exit(1).
  * responder_get_request raises on a socket error (a closed or never
    connected responder) instead of logging and returning, which made
    the caller's listener loop spin without yielding, starving its event
    loop. Malformed requests and raising callbacks are handled as before.
  * send_request takes timeout= (seconds, default 100) for the send and
    the reply together, and returns None when it passes: asking a service
    that was not running used to block for good.
  * A cancelled reply() or responder_get_request() always stops: pynng
    operations are shielded from cancellation (about 1 cancellation in
    1000 used to hang on a lost NNG callback), and the socket or context
    is closed instead.
  * NngBusHub counts a message as sent only after asend() succeeds, so a
    failing link no longer reports itself healthy.
  * NngBusHub delivers every frame: JSON that is not an object, and bytes
    that are not UTF-8, were counted and dropped; they now arrive as
    {"raw_data": ...}, as non-JSON text already did.
  * SignalEngine's SIGTERM/SIGINT handlers call sys.exit(), not the site
    builtin exit(), which python -S and frozen builds do not define.
  * NngBusHub.enable_auto_ping()/disable_auto_ping() take effect at once
    on a running hub, instead of after the current interval (10 s).
  * NngBusHub.start() returns, with an error logged, once its bus socket
    closes; it used to keep running with no bus.
  * SignalEngine's SIGTERM/SIGINT handlers exit with self.exit_status()
    (0 unless a subclass overrides it), so a service that stops itself on
    a failure can exit non-zero and be restarted by Restart=on-failure.
  * New cuemsutils.tools.AsyncCommsThread, absorbed from cuems-engine so
    cuems-nodeconf stops keeping a copy: the daemon thread that runs a
    service's NNG event loop. A task that raises, or an essential() task
    that returns, ends the communications and calls on_comms_ended();
    stop() blocks until the thread is gone, and is idempotent.
  * Packaging: debian/ lives on the working branch. After this merge
    debian/bookworm is contained in it; that line may keep releasing
    0.1.0rcN until 0.1.1 is published, and each such release is merged in
    the same way. The packaging-rc14 tag this entry used to mention was
    never created.

  Carried from the folded 0.1.0rc16 entry:
  * Schema renames, none of which invalidate a document on disk:
    outputs.xsd becomes hardware_outputs.xsd, with its root element
    (CuemsHardwareOutputs), its type (HardwareOutputsType) and its schema key
    renamed with it. This resolves an audit finding where two schemas declared
    OutputsType in the same namespace with different content.
    project_mappings.xsd's NodeType becomes NodeMappingType, leaving
    network_map.xsd's NodeType as the only declaration of that name; type
    names are schema-internal, so no document changes.
  * Schema field removals, each with a registered conversion so documents in
    the field still load:
    settings.xsd drops audioplayer/audio_cards and dmxplayer/universes --
    counts restating another document's content, read by nothing anywhere in
    the ecosystem. settings documents move to doc_version 2.
    hardware_outputs.xsd drops default_video_output and default_audio_output
    -- authored choices already declared in project_mappings. That schema
    moves to doc_version 2. Verified against a real production settings.xml.
  * The generated reference settings document is corrected against the two
    audited production machines. All four player sections previously named
    /usr/bin/cuems-player, a binary that has never existed and is absent from
    both machines; they now name cuems-videocomposer, cuems-audioplayer,
    jack-volume and cuems-dmxplayer respectively. editor_url becomes
    formitgo.local, the brand hostname operators actually use. The generator
    also emits the optional knobs (osc_port, output_latency_ms) that it
    filtered out before.
  * An empty <node_list/> now raises ValueError rather than TypeError, so the
    failure names the document instead of the machinery.
  * An atomic save no longer discards the target file's mode.
  * /etc/cuems first install (feature 011). The six XSD files ship to
    /usr/share/cuems/schemas and are copied to /etc/cuems on every configure
    (never a conffile), replacing cuems-common's mirror; that package hands
    the two paths over in 1.3.0-23 and this one Breaks: cuems-common
    (<< 1.3.0-23~). The three documents a node needs are generated at build
    from the schemas and the new seed-values file (system-defaults.toml,
    package data; a /etc/cuems/defaults.d overlay for sites), carrying the
    reserved sentinel identity so the build is reproducible, and postinst
    creates them in /etc/cuems only where absent — running the new
    cuems-init-node under a 60 s timeout to mint one uuid4 and write the
    three as one atomic set, falling back to the pristine placeholders with
    a NOT PROVISIONED warning and always exiting 0, since this is the base
    package of the stack. An existing file is never modified; identity
    survives upgrade, --reinstall and remove, and only purge removes the
    nine paths this package placed. cuems-init-node re-provisions with
    identity and hand edits preserved (--reset returns to defaults), and
    --check reports the four identity locations with exit 0/1/2/3. The
    Avahi record is rendered from settings.xml by cuems-nodeconf (its
    feature 003); cuems-config-node no longer mints.
  * Packaging hygiene: debhelper-compat (= 13) replaces debian/compat 11,
    Standards-Version 4.6.2, README.Debian rewritten.


  Carried from the folded retrospective 0.1.0rc15 entry (refactor work
  recorded under that number; the number belongs to the released build
  below):
  * New entry point: cuems-convert-documents, an offline batch upgrade for
    XML documents, installed into the shared venv alongside the library. It
    backs up each document before rewriting and treats a backup failure as
    fatal for that document alone.
  * Reading became strict. Every document load now runs structural and
    semantic validation: a valid document loads, a version-old one converts
    IN MEMORY with the file on disk untouched, a repairable violation loads
    with the field repaired to its declared default, an unrepairable one
    raises, and a document newer than the library raises distinguishably.
    Operators get a report naming every repair rather than a silent
    substitution.
  * Documents carry a doc_version marker, per schema, with a conversion
    registered for every version step. Absent means version 1, so nothing on
    disk is invalidated by its introduction.
  * network_map.xsd: <node_type>, free text carrying NodeType.master /
    NodeType.slave, becomes <node_role>, typed controller/node/firstrun.
    DEPLOYED MAPS MUST BE CONVERTED -- both audited production machines were
    still carrying the old vocabulary at the time of writing.
  * The library gained its first write path for network_map.xml, and the
    node object model moved in from cuems-nodeconf.
  * One public API across the library: load/save/validate/from_json/to_json/
    to_wire on the script object, configuration accessors answering with
    objects, and cuemsutils.errors as the one public error module. Six
    retired entry points still resolve and warn; they are REMOVED IN v0.1.2,
    which is why every consumer pins << 0.1.2~.
  * DmxUniverse no longer silently stores unconverted channel data when a
    per-entry conversion fails; it raises DmxChannelDecodeError naming the
    universe and the failing entry.
  * Media duration is typed as a timecode, and the unused fade-profile
    surface is deleted.

