cuems-utils (0.1.0rc16) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Merge main into debian/bookworm (0.1.0rc16, 869fej07m): media cues
    without a usable media block. MediaCue.media_status() classifies a
    cue's media as none / invalid / ok without touching the raising
    file_name property; CueList.get_media (editor path) raises a named
    ValueError for an invalid block instead of a bare KeyError 'file_name'
    and skips a None block with a warning; CuemsScript.get_own_media
    (engine path) never raises - both shapes are logged and skipped, so a
    legacy <Media/> project still loads and that cue fails at arm as
    before. Same code as cuemsutils 0.1.0rc16 on PyPI (tag v0.1.0rc16).

